   "source": [
    "# Exploratory Data Analysis: My Iris Garden Journal\n",
    "\n",
    "Hey there! 👋 Welcome to my little data adventure with the famous Iris dataset. I've always been fascinated by flowers (maybe it's because I keep killing my houseplants), so this dataset feels oddly personal to me. Let's dive in and see what secrets these flowers are hiding!\n",
    "\n",
    "> *Note: While this is the classic Iris dataset, I'm pretending these are measurements from my obsessive flower-tracking hobby. Don't judge my hobbies!*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Let's get our tools ready! Importing the usual suspects\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "# Setting up pretty plots because life's too short for ugly graphs\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8')\n",
    "sns.set_palette(\"husl\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Loading the Iris dataset - pretend I measured these myself!\n",
    "# (Spoiler: I didn't. I killed three succulents trying.)\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import load_iris\n",
    "iris = load_iris()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Creating a DataFrame because spreadsheets are life\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(data=iris.data, columns=iris.feature_names)\n",
    "df['species'] = pd.Categorical.from_codes(iris.target, iris.target_names)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Let's meet our floral subjects!\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🌸 Meet the Flowers\n",
    "\n",
    "Here we have three lovely species:\n",
    "- **Setosa**: The dainty one with petite petals\n",
    "- **Versicolor**: The versatile middle child\n",
    "- **Virginica**: The showy diva with big, bold petals\n",
    "\n",
    "I've named them all after my exes. Just kidding... mostly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Basic info about our floral friends\n",
    "print(\"📊 Dataset Overview\")\n",
    "print(f\"We have {df.shape[0]} flower measurements\")\n",
    print(f\"Each flower has {df.shape[1]-1} measurements (plus species)\")\n",
    print()\n",
    "print(\"📋 Column names:\")\n",
    "for col in df.columns:\n",
    "    print(f\"  - {col}\")\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"📈 Data types:\")\n",
    "print(df.dtypes)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Let's get to know our flowers better with some stats\n",
    "print(\"📊 Summary Statistics\")\n",
    "display(df.describe())\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"🌸 Species distribution:\")\n",
    "print(df['species'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔍 Missing Data Investigation\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's check if any of our flower measurements went missing (probably off enjoying photosynthesis somewhere):"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Checking for missing values\n",
    "missing_counts = df.isnull().sum()\n",
    "print(\"🔍 Missing values per column:\")\n",
    "display(missing_counts)\n",
    "print()\n",
    "if missing_counts.sum() == 0:\n",
    "    print(\"✅ Hooray! No missing data - our flowers were all present and accounted for!\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"⚠️  Uh oh, we have some missing data to deal with.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
